NAME
    gcloud alpha number-registry custom-ranges - manage custom range resources

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha number-registry custom-ranges COMMAND [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Manage custom range resources.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     create
        (ALPHA) Create a custom range resource.

     delete
        (ALPHA) Delete a single custom range resource.

     describe
        (ALPHA) Gets details of a single custom range resource.

     find-free-ip-ranges
        (ALPHA) Find free IP ranges in a custom range.

     list
        (ALPHA) List custom range resources.

     show-utilization
        (ALPHA) Show utilization of a custom range.

     update
        (ALPHA) Update the parameters of a single custom range resource.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist.

